					<dc:identifier>http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2000/2792/article/2</dc:identifier><dc:title>The Fixed Penalty Order 2000</dc:title><dc:subject>Road traffic offences</dc:subject><dc:subject>Vehicles</dc:subject><dc:subject scheme="SIheading">CRIMINAL LAW, ENGLAND AND WALES</dc:subject><dc:subject scheme="SIheading">CRIMINAL LAW, SCOTLAND</dc:subject><dc:publisher>Statute Law Database</dc:publisher><dc:modified>2025-07-01</dc:modified><dc:contributor>Expert Participation</dc:contributor><dct:valid>2021-10-31</dct:valid>
					<dc:description>This Order prescribes fixed penalties for fixed penalty offences. The prescribed penalties replace those prescribed for England and Wales by the Fixed Penalty Order 1992 (S.I. 1992/346) and for Scotland by the Fixed Penalty (Increase) (Scotland) Order 1992 (S.I. 1992/435 (S. 50)).</dc:description>
